 "notes": "No submission is AC (all WA, RTE or TLE), so orig.cpp is a reference written for the port. Primeness is at most T = floor(N^2/2) - 1, the maximum total variation, and for N >= 6 an all-prime path cannot reach T (the forced alternating shape puts every peak on one parity), so orig.cpp builds a T - 1 path as two parity-class Hamiltonian paths (Posa rotation-extension) over the prime-difference graph and aborts unless the total is exactly T - 1; N <= 21 comes from an exact bitmask DP. Checked: primeness equals the dmopc21c5p5 AC 4223887 for every N in 1..=100, and every N in 22..=5000 and 99800..=100000 plus 500 random N up to 1e5 reaches T - 1 in under 1 s. Any maximum permutation is accepted, so checker.py (shared with dmopc21c5p5) compares primeness with the reference's."
